WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
How does stakeholder research turn
interviews into usable direction?

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.420
A list of names is like a map with no
terrain.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.220
It tells you who is on paper, but not
where the difficult crossings are.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.060
First name the decision.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.380
Then distinguish people affected by it,
people who will implement it and

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.540
people who will make it.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.880
Ask open questions about priorities,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.180
constraints and what each group thinks is
being missed.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.360
Imagine a public institution planning a
service change.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.420
Staff may see an operational bottleneck,
partners may see a handoff problem

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.200
and community members may see an access
barrier.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.520
The report should show those differences,

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.580
not force a false consensus.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.760
A few interviews provide depth, not a
population percentage.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.180
PRC Impact helps organizations connect
stakeholder perspectives to

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.960
decisions. Bring your decision and
timeline to prcimpact.com,

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.740
or call

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:58.000
334-429-6994.
